{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/814458-kinain-character-generation-rules-help","id":814458,"title":"Kinain Character Generation Rules - Help?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Changeling: The Dreaming"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-01-22T14:37:32-08:00","id":814458,"title":"Kinain Character Generation Rules - Help?","content":"Hey guys, I'm having trouble understanding some of the rules around Kinain character generation. Specifically around fae gifts and fae backgrounds.<br /> <br /> Character creation rules state that you get 5 points for backgrounds and 5 points for fae gifts. Backgrounds are then split between &quot;fae&quot; backgrounds and &quot;mortal&quot; backgrounds. It is stated that a kinain may not have more fae backgrounds than points of faerie blood, and that a kinain may not have more than 5 fae gifts (it seems to suggest at the start this is regardless of fae blood, but the fae blood background says that's the limit on fae gifts but mentions nothing about backgrounds).<br /> <br /> Here are my questions:<br /> <br /> 1) Is the limit on the number of fae backgrounds inclusive of faerie blood itself? Or does it mean in addition to faerie blood?<br /> <br /> 2) This reads to me as though the 5 points for backgrounds must be split between mortal and fae backgrounds while the 5 points for fae gifts must be spend on the merit-like fae gifts with set points values. However, the example characters seem to allow the fae gift points to be spend on fae backgrounds as well? Is this effectively a 10 point pool where no more than 5 of them can be spent on mortal backgrounds?<br /> <br /> 3) Is your level of fae blood the limit on BOTH fae backgrounds and fae gifts each? Cumulatively? One? The other? <br /> <br /> And this is without touching the confusing information where it is indicated that Kinain have 15 freebie points in some places but 21 freebie points at others.<br /> <br /> Can anyone shed any light on this?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":187,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/187-beccatoria","user":"beccatoria","date":". 01-22-2016, 05:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/187-beccatoria","name":"beccatoria","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar187_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-23T06:40:07-08:00","id":814811,"title":"","content":"The character creation section in <i>The Enchanted</i> is a total mess. I'll just get that out of the way. I actually just use the simplified version of the system here: <a href=\"http://changeling.wenchipedia.com/kinainchart.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://changeling.wenchipedia.com/kinainchart.html</a>. It makes the most sense.<br /> <br /> But, for clarity, <i>The Enchanted</i> conflates Fae Gifts with Fae Backgrounds by mistake, it seems. The book can't work out if Fae Backgrounds are a type of Fae Gift, or whether they're something else.<br /> <br /> The character creation summary also fails to mention that you get a free dot in the Faerie Blood Background (although it does mention this under the description of the trait), nor does it say whether this counts towards your limit for Fae Backgrounds and Fae Gifts. I would therefore rule that you get it for free and Faerie Blood doesn't count towards your limit. Your remaining five dots in Backgrounds can be spent on mortal or Fae Backgrounds as you wish, including on raising your Faerie Blood Background. But the character can't have more Fae Backgrounds than he has dots in the Faerie Blood Background, so if you don't spend Background dots to increase your Faerie Blood trait, you can only take one Fae Background (although you could opt to spend the remaining five of your Background dots in that single trait). You could only take one Fae Gift in addition, because that is also capped in the same way.<br /> <br /> To further complicate things, the book does refer to Fae Backgrounds as a type of Fae Gift and it seems to imply that neither Fae Gifts nor Fae Backgrounds can number more than your Faerie Blood score, but together they can't number more than five. So a character with Faerie Blood 3 could have two Fae Gifts and three Fae Backgrounds (with five dots to allocate to each type), or vice versa, but not three of each, because that would put her above the five trait cap. Yes, I know, it's overly complicated.<br /> <br /> A generous ST might allow points from Fae Gifts to be spent on further Fae Backgrounds, since there's a lot of overlap between them, but it's technically not allowed by the RAW. I tend to require the two pools to stay separate, but ignore the cap on Fae Backgrounds (although I keep the cap for Fae Gifts).<br /> <br /> Like all characters that start with mortal levels of Attributes and Abilities, kinain get 21 Freebies. This is the same as ghouls, dhampyrs, sorcerers, etc.<br /> <br /> Another flaw in the layout is that you have to go all the way back to pp.13-14 to get the starting Tempers for each character based on their Age (Seeming).<br /> <br /> As I said, though, use the chart above. It's so much easier to understand. (Note that it too ignores the limit on Fae Backgrounds altogether, but not on Fae Gifts.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":5291,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","user":"adambeyoncelowe","date":". 07-07-2016, 02:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-23T07:16:51-08:00","id":814822,"title":"","content":"PRAISE BE, AN ANSWER! <br /> <br /> Thanks for the clarification - I was never heavily into the other games so I wasn't aware other mortal level characters also got additional freebies, or that probably wouldn't have confused me so much. But yeah. I won't say that the character creation is more poorly edited than Inanimae, but it <i>is</i> more confusing because it's harder to use common sense to work out. <br /> <br /> From looking at the example characters, in general their freebie setups, and initial points buys seem to be a mess, but one thing that <i>is</i> consistent is that the &quot;no more fae gifts than dots in faerie blood&quot; thing seems to be applied across backgrounds and gifts as a cumulative. So like, if you had Faerie Blood 3 you could have one fae background and two fae gifts or vice versa but not two of each. <br /> <br /> But honestly ideologically that's a mess because the backgrounds are so poorly differentiated from gifts in terms of what they <i>do</i>? Like I know backgrounds have always encompassed both material and social resources <i>and</i> more mystical advantages, but it's particularly messy when you bring the concepts of fae gifts into play. Like, why is Feth Fiada a background, but Spearman's Shield a gift? I can understand the idea of limiting the number of magical gifts by the strength of your fae heritage. But while it'd make sense to apply that rule to backgrounds that are inherent to the Kinain because of that heritage - like Kenning, for instance - it doesn't make a whole lot of sense to apply it to something like Dross. Which is access to a fae resource, sure, but would presumably be acquired through social relationships and have nothing to do with your genetic capacity for, like, magical faerie stuff? OY. <br /> <br /> Which, obviously, is not aimed at you! <br /> <br /> What I mean to say is, removing the limit on backgrounds and simply using one pool for each type of gift seems by far the most sensible solution. Most of the fae backgrounds kinain can access are more social than innately magical anyway, so they're not going to end up &quot;cheating&quot; their way to a ton more magical abilities than they &quot;should&quot; have by doing that anyway. At most they'll have some extra help with sensing glamour and hiding in the mists, and a more developed social network in Kithain society than one might expect. <br /> <br /> Also - I was asking for two reasons - firstly because C20 has the glamour running in our game group again and we wanna start a new C:tD game soon and I've always thought it'd be fun to play a Changeling, but also because I'm working on a spreadsheet-based character generator and this solution will make my life immeasurably easier in that regard...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/187-beccatoria","name":"beccatoria","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar187_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-23T14:50:20-08:00","id":815053,"title":"","content":"Yes, it's a mess. The chart at the link above, however, is a lot clearer, and does seem to fit the RAW.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-23T15:27:33-08:00","id":815070,"title":"","content":"If it helps, I also have my own system for generating kinain who are also mages or sorcerers (in theory, the same template could be applied to ghouls, kinfolk and other humans, too, although I doubt it would be appropriate for the Imbued):<br /> <br /> <b>Character creation:</b><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"> The character creation rules in </span></span></span><i>The Enchanted</i><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"> are for mortal kinain only. You should create your character as a mage or hedge mage first, and then use Freebies to 'add on' the fae characteristics. You should consult </span></span></span><i>The Enchanted</i><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"> for the specific rules on kinain-specific traits.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Apply the following template to modify your kinain character:</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">1. Create a mage/hedge mage character as normal, remembering that chimerical reality and/or their fae blood will probably be incorporated into their paradigm. The character's Avatar essence might also be informed by their fae heritage (a Sluagh-descended kinain may be Primordial, while a Satyr's relative may be Dynamic).</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">2. Take the 4-point Merit: Faerie Blood. This will grant the character a single dot in the Faerie Blood Background. Alternatively, you can take the Faerie Affinity Merit, which gives you a lower Banality (one dot lower than normal) and makes changelings more friendly, but does not allow the character to take any Fae Gifts or Kinain Backgrounds, nor to interact with chimerical reality.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">3. Note your Age (Seeming) and Seelie/Unseelie Legacies. Pick a Heritage (Kith). Your Glamour and Banality ratings are determined by your Age (Seeming), as per p.13-14 of <i>The Enchanted</i>. Base Willpower remains the same for the original character template.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">4. You start with no free Fae Gifts or Kinain Backgrounds. You can spend Freebies to take any Fae Gifts and Kinain Backgrounds you like (provided you already have the Faerie Blood Merit), but the number of either kind of trait you can take is limited to your total dots in the Faerie Blood Background. So if you have Faerie Blood 5, you can take up to five separate Fae Gifts and up to five separate Kinain Backgrounds. These tricks are Paradox-free. Kinain Backgrounds can only be bought from your Freebie pool, rather than from your normal Background dots.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">5. Fae Marks can be taken to gain additional Freebie Points.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">The Kinain Background Fith-Fath costs 1-5 points (based on the dice pool for Fith-Fath) and can only be taken by hedge mages.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Full list of Fae Gifts: <a href=\"http://changeling.wenchipedia.com/faegifts.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://changeling.wenchipedia.com/faegifts.html</a></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Full list of Kinain Backgrounds: <a href=\"http://changeling.wenchipedia.com/kinainbackgrounds.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://changeling.wenchipedia.com/ki...ckgrounds.html</a></span></span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}